STEP 6: CRITICAL DIAGNOSIS
================================================================================

PROBLEM IDENTIFIED:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Test A: Val loss = 0.19, Val acc = 87.9% (GOOD)
Test B: Val loss = 17.7, Val acc = 0.0% (FAILURE)

BOTH tests have:
  - 0% target OOV
  - Same model architecture
  - Same tokenizer
  - Same training steps (500)
  - Same hyperparameters

ONLY difference:
  - Test A: Val sequences = subset of train (100% n-gram overlap)
  - Test B: Val sequences = different stories (0% n-gram overlap)

CRITICAL QUESTION:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why does the model achieve 17.7 loss on Test B when target OOV = 0%?

Expected behavior with 0% target OOV:
  - Random baseline: loss ≈ ln(4000) ≈ 8.29
  - Observed Test B: loss = 17.7 (WORSE than random!)

This suggests the model is NOT just failing to generalize.
The model is outputting WRONG distributions that are WORSE than random.

